<title>THAILAND: RESEARCH ALERT-Robinson rated &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Robinson rated &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia Equity Ltd on Monday rated Robinson Department Store Plc &quot;buy&quot; on expectation the firm would post special gains of over 700 million baht ($26.9 million) in the fourth quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;ROBINS will book over 700 million baht in extraordinary gains during the fourth quarter from the sale of its Save One shares,&quot; said Asia Equity in a research report.  </p>
<p>Asia Equity said the 700 million baht special gains were higher than its earlier projected figure of 500 million baht.</p>
<p>It said Robinson Department could post another 100-200 million baht extraordinary gains by 1999 if its Save One unit met sale and profit margin targets.</p>
<p>Robinson Department rose 0.25 baht to 23.00 at 0904 GMT on Monday.</p>
<p>($US1 = 26 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
